{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/845254-whats-mist-caused-forgetfulness-like","id":845254,"title":"Whats Mist Caused Forgetfulness like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-10T14:03:11-08:00","id":845254,"title":"Whats Mist Caused Forgetfulness like?","content":"when a changelings undone, or when a enchantment ends, whats it like the incomplete fragmentary memorys, especialy as they ONLY involve the aspects involving the supernatural, <br /> <br /> Does a childlings adventures in the dreaming seem like a &quot;Imagination game&quot; He and his friends played?<br /> <br /> in particular ideas how one whos had almost no &quot;Human life&quot; to speak of for most of their life will fill things in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T05:39:56-08:00","id":845567,"title":"","content":"It fills in with vague and fuzzy memories like the &quot;unreliable eyewitness&quot; effect in most circumstances. Very susceptible to suggestion, I imagine, as it's a blank spot that your brain knows SHOULD have something there and seeks to use its pattern-recognition ability to regenerate, so it builds from your own imagination an <u>acceptably realistic</u> (i.e. banal) explanation for what happened, and will probably happily incorporate details provided by others as &quot;reminders.&quot; (This could lead to interesting effects for any mortals who are immersed enough in other supernatural beings' subcultures that they might, for instance, see a Pooka using Gimmix as a gangrel using his shadow to reach out and snatch the object.)<br /> <br /> For more involved things, it will become filled in with &quot;that game we used to play as kids&quot; or &quot;that LARP we do.&quot; Or, possibly, glossed over entirely differently: that gang you ran with, or those parties you used to attend. To some degree, you might remember full events relatively accurately...just only what your mortal body was really doing. Where that doesn't make sense (because your mortal body was engaged in high class activities in a run-down warehouse, for example), it might edit the location (you were at a hotel convention hall, perhaps). If you had no mortal life up to that point, then you'll either feel you've squandered your life on a make-believe that you just can't sustain anymore, or you'll have a very boring life of nothing much happening where you had some regular, banal but mildly entertaining habit of getting together with a group of friends to do...stuff. If that was your day job, you may even now want to actually get a real life and stop being a waste of space layabout with no job. Just like your parents have always wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T18:50:26-07:00","id":846862,"title":"","content":"And then if you get your memorys back you'll probaly go back to being a waste of space layabout with no job. Hopefully with some plan in place to soften the blow to mom and dad, though no guarantees...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T19:49:04-07:00","id":847479,"title":"","content":"That last part is something I never really understood. The idea that holding down a steady job is a straight line to Forgetting just doesn't make any sense. Yes, going through the motions of Office Job TM carries with it a certain amount of Banality, but so does sitting in your parents' basement getting high and playing video games day after day. This also ignores the idea that someone can derive personal and creative fulfillment from any sort of adult responsibility. &quot;Growing up&quot; and becoming a Grump carries with it a new set of challenges. You have to learn to live with a little more Banality and you have to find some new ways of getting Glamour. Those that don't adapt with ultimately fall into Forgetting, but those that can make the transition have no reason not to enjoy long Changeling lives. <br /> <br /> Changeling is first and foremost a game about being young, and its something I consider a feature rather than a bug. Nobody likes a Peter Pan complex though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:13:05-07:00","id":847661,"title":"","content":"For me it depends on when in their life the changeling becomes undone. If it's at an early age, the individual can &quot;put away childish things&quot; and continue to live a comfortable life, only duller and with less potential than before.<br /> <br /> If the changeling becomes undone later in life, I think the results would look more like dementia or Alzheimer's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:35:07-07:00","id":847679,"title":"","content":"oh thought on creating another thread for this, but on Enchanted? A question tokens have to have been &quot;Created by the changeling&quot; at what point is it something ive created as a sidhe might want only the finest tokens for his personal entourage... but isnt able to craft jewelry himself.<br /> <br /> is Wrapping a package yourself, enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 03-15-2016, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T16:33:42-07:00","id":850848,"title":"","content":"A thought strikes me now that I'm <i>really</i> curious about<b></b>: What happens to someone who gets undone but is still in contact with <i>other</i> supernaturals? If your mind is already going through hella cognitive dissonance dealing with the sudden huge gaps of memory about everything faerie-related, what happens if you already knew that Bob down the hall is a vampire, or that you should stay away from those standing stones in the park because werewolves? What goes through your head if your dead sibling shows up to brag about their awesome new private-eye job at this startup downtown? Would Bob or your dead sister notice that something's seriously wrong? Would it be possible for a very strong-willed person to figure it out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2444-lindhrive","name":"Lindhrive","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T04:36:04-07:00","id":851658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lindhrive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/845254-whats-mist-caused-forgetfulness-like?p=850848#post850848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought strikes me now that I'm <i>really</i> curious about<b></b>: What happens to someone who gets undone but is still in contact with <i>other</i> supernaturals? If your mind is already going through hella cognitive dissonance dealing with the sudden huge gaps of memory about everything faerie-related, what happens if you already knew that Bob down the hall is a vampire, or that you should stay away from those standing stones in the park because werewolves? What goes through your head if your dead sibling shows up to brag about their awesome new private-eye job at this startup downtown? Would Bob or your dead sister notice that something's seriously wrong? Would it be possible for a very strong-willed person to figure it out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even supernaturals are affected by the Mists. So you still wouldn't remember your fae life, even in the face of other supers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T06:47:33-07:00","id":851714,"title":"","content":"so does a changeling kinfolk go back to doing normal sept dutys after the undoing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T07:32:42-07:00","id":851731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/845254-whats-mist-caused-forgetfulness-like?p=851714#post851714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so does a changeling kinfolk go back to doing normal sept dutys after the undoing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a changeling kinfolk heavily involved with shifter society would be far more likely to fall to bedlam than banality. As for what would happen if the changeling is undone, it'll depend on if it's a Werewolf game with a changeling guest star or Changeling game with some werewolves sprinkled in.<br /> <br /> If its the former, yeah, that's probably what would happen. The changeling would have no memory it's glorious deeds along side the Garou, and probably serves as a potent and sad reminder to the werewolves of the sept of the danger posed by the Weaver.<br /> <br /> If it's the latter, the Mists might guide the former changeling to a mundane life, free of any supernatural influence. The changeling's werewolf friends, being wayward creatures of dream themselves, probably don't notice their faerie companion is no longer with them. Some event might trigger a memory in them - &quot;Hey, what ever happened to that troll that used to run with us? He was a great fighter.&quot; The others might shrug and reminisce for a bit, and then get back to more pressing matters at hand without giving the changeling a second thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T11:11:41-07:00","id":851880,"title":"","content":"Pooka Two questions if I could? <br /> <br /> One Any idea if house Gwydion will ransom a Iron Paladin whos captured?<br /> <br /> Two Ideas on how Boggans arent Banal when they devote themselves to menial work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T18:57:24-07:00","id":852171,"title":"","content":"The other option for the Mists is to erase the <i>mundane</i> aspects from the memory, turning it into something completely unbelievable as anything other than a delusion or dream or drug trip. You forget that the clurichaun (leprechaun) is actually Brien, your neighbor. Instead, you remember your adventures with &quot;O'Brien&quot;, a tiny figure dressed in green and clover, with an atrocious Irish brogue. Something that no &quot;responsible&quot; person would ever take seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/845254-whats-mist-caused-forgetfulness-like?p=851880#post851880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . Ideas on how Boggans arent Banal when they devote themselves to menial work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're getting hung up on the idea of chores as drudgery. Remember, Boggans actually enjoy cooking, cleaning, making shoes . . . and often add an element of whimsy to the experience. Mary Poppins, singing the children's bedroom clean, is a good example of a Boggan using her kith's birthright. So is Rumpelstiltskin, who spun a warehouse of straw into thread* in a single night, before wagering his pay on a guessing game. <br /> <br /> <br /> *turning it into gold takes other magic, of course<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 03-23-2016, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T19:01:51-07:00","id":852174,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Rumplestillskin, Would like a magic that could achieve his transformation TRUE Transformation not an illusion...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T05:44:20-07:00","id":852352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/845254-whats-mist-caused-forgetfulness-like?p=851880#post851880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Any idea if house Gwydion will ransom a Iron Paladin whos captured?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it make for a fun game? If so, sure. If not, nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two Ideas on how Boggans arent Banal when they devote themselves to menial work? </div> </div> </div>What One Vorlon said. Chores can be fun. Seeing a yard transform as you care for it and the gardens take shape is an almost magical experience. Cleaning a house - turning it from a drab and ho-hum sight into something glorious can be inspiring. Sure, it's a lot of work, but so is writing, sculpting, or painting if you want to excel at them. It's not the amount of work involved. It's more your mindset about the work. Glamour can be found just about anywhere as long as you're willing to approach it with an open mind and a sense of wonder. The problem is that banality prevents most people from doing that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of Rumplestillskin, Would like a magic that could achieve his transformation TRUE Transformation not an illusion... </div> </div> </div>Right now, Primal or Metamorphosis could probably do it. That answer might change when C20 is released <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T13:28:49-07:00","id":852565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/845254-whats-mist-caused-forgetfulness-like?p=852352#post852352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it make for a fun game? If so, sure. If not, nope.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I meant, do you think it would be Charachteristic for them..<